# ERP Hajj — Project Context

ERP Hajj is a **multi-tenant Arabic enterprise web platform** for managing and governing Hajj campaign companies (شركات وحملات الحج). Each tenant is an independent campaign company with strictly isolated data.

## Fixed facts

- MVP scope is **fixed** (21 modules): auth, dashboard, users, roles, permissions, org structure, employees, supervisors, contracts, meetings, decisions, tasks, documents, warehouses, basic inventory, custodies, assets, MVP notifications, audit trail, multi-tenant foundation, required settings. See `docs/00-project/MVP_SCOPE.md`.
- Domain separations: Decisions ≠ Tasks; Assets ≠ Custodies; Inventory items ≠ Assets; Supervisor = Employee with supervisory classification (one identity record).
- Four core workflows in `docs/01-business/CORE_WORKFLOWS.md` (governance chain, contract lifecycle, asset/custody lifecycle, inventory transactions).
- Stack: Laravel 12 (PHP 8.2+), Sanctum, MySQL, Redis when required, queues, REST `/api/v1`, Policies/Gates, Form Requests, API Resources | Vue 3, TypeScript, Vite, Pinia, Vue Router, TanStack Query, Tailwind CSS.
- Architecture: monorepo, modular monolith, API-first, multi-tenant (single DB, shared schema, `tenant_id`).
- Web only now; API reusable by future Android/iOS apps. Do not build mobile apps.
- Arabic first, RTL first, sidebar on the right, responsive desktop-first, light theme, deep green primary + gold accent.
- Two developers via GitHub PRs (`main` + `develop`, Conventional Commits) — see `docs/00-project/TEAM_AND_GIT_WORKFLOW.md`.

## Working rules

- **Read the relevant documentation before implementation** — start with `docs/09-modules/<module>/` for the module being built.
- The `docs/` tree is the source of truth. If code and docs disagree, raise it — do not silently pick one.
- Anything marked **TBD** is undecided: **stop and mark the ambiguity when a business decision is required** — never assume an answer.

## Completion report (mandatory)

Before completing any implementation task, print: files changed · migrations added · endpoints added · permissions added · audit events added · tests added · documentation updated · assumptions · remaining risks.
